# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# WITHOUT THIS FILE THE BUILD CONTEXT IS ABOUT 8 GB. `.gitignore` does not apply to
# `docker build`, so `COPY . .` otherwise sweeps in data/ (1.5 GB), .venv/ (6.3 GB),
# artifacts/ (143 MB) and wandb/ -- all of which are gitignored precisely because they do
# not belong in a distributable. The resulting image is enormous, the build is slow, and
# the layer cache is invalidated by any run output.
#
# Keep this file in step with .gitignore. The release verification asserts that a clean
# clone carries no data or artifacts (`no-data-committed`); this is the same rule for the
# image, and nothing enforces it automatically.

# --- data and results: never in an image; mount them as volumes instead ---
data/
artifacts/
dist/
wandb/
outputs/
multirun/

# --- environments and build products ---
.venv/
venv/
build/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- model weights ---
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.gguf

# --- caches ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# --- secrets: belt and braces. These must never reach an image layer, because a layer
#     is readable even after a later layer deletes the file. ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
credentials.json

# --- git: the image does not need history, and it is the largest thing left.
#     RunContext reads the SHA at run time; pass it as a build arg if a build needs it. ---
.git/
.github/

# --- editors / os ---
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# --- exceptions: these ARE needed in the image ---
# tests/fixtures/ carries the quickstart fixture the image scores at build time, and
# tests/golden/ carries what it is asserted against. Neither matches a rule above, but
# both are load-bearing for `RUN python scripts/14_quickstart.py` -- do not add a broad
# `tests/` exclusion without moving them.
